[Music]  that's thirteen-year-old Gianna Bryant  showing off her skills in a moving video  her mom Vanessa Bryant shared on  Instagram Monday morning the footage  brings Gigi's natural athleticism to  life  and highlights the special bond she  shared with her dad Kobe Bryant with the  video vanessa pent an emotional caption  about her state following the loss of  her husband and 13 year old daughter the  37 year old writes in part quote my  brain refuses to accept that both Kobe  and Gigi are gone I can't process both  at the same time adding it's like I'm  trying to process Kobe being gone but my  body refuses to accept my gg will never  come back to me it feels wrong GG's a  basketball player she is that she's in  it does she have that inner focus like  her daddy  yeah she's she's just don't go killer  out there yeah at both ends of the floor  she plays defense as well as offense man  she competes Vanessa continues quote why  should I be able to wake up another day  when my baby girl isn't being able to  have that opportunity I'm so mad she had  so much life to live god I wish they  were here and this nightmare would be  over praying for all of the victims of  this horrible tragedy please continue to  pray for all Vanessa  ends her post beloved by fans around the  world  Kobe Bryant had transcended the game  he embodied excellence achieved an  aspiration for millions of fans  everywhere  [Music]  Koby Gianna and seven others died in a  helicopter crash in Calabasas California  on January 26 Vanessa  broke her silence three days later  posting this family photo on Instagram  since then she shared a number of  tributes including photos and videos  from the memorial held at GG school he  also posted this pic of the LA Lakers  tribute to the black mamba and his  mamacita duty game over the weekend  Vanessa shared an adorable video of her  seven month old daughter Capri riding my  cocoa beam she looks just like my Gigi  with her daddy's eyes and posted about a  public memorial that's being held for  Kobe and Gianna at the Staples Center on  February 24 my mentality is it's a way  of life a source tells et that vanessa  has been surrounded by her family and  friends but she feels almost numb to  everything she married Kobe when she was  18 and she never expected to live life  without him so it's going to take time  the source adds quote right now she's  taking time to be with her girls  responsibilities always inspire and try  to take some of the life lessons that we  have learned and share those with the  next generation so that they can start  their journey with a Lego

